{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Kmbyfp7jaAmMFJp8gkasR","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"artifact_id\": \"309dcc22-361b-4448-a2e5-3fbd2efecbe4\",\n \"artifact_type\": \"property_result\",\n \"producer_agent\": \"worker\",\n \"skill_used\": \"coolorbit.property_result\",\n \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n \"payload\": {\n  \"candidate\": \"silicon (diamond cubic)\",\n  \"family\": \"group-IV semiconductor\",\n  \"tier\": \"trust\",\n  \"property\": \"lattice_constant\",\n  \"value\": 5.456,\n  \"units\": \"angstrom\",\n  \"uncertainty\": 0.03,\n  \"method\": {\n   \"engine\": \"ASE 3.29 EquationOfState + mace-torch 0.3.15 ASE calculator (GPU, ALCHEMI toolkit environment)\",\n   \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (2023-12-03-mace-128-L1_epoch-199), float64; trained on MPtrj (PBE/PBE+U)\",\n   \"protocol\": \"static 0 K E(V) scan: 11 isotropic strains of the 8-atom cubic cell, a in [0.96,1.04]*a_guess; Birch-Murnaghan fit (cross-checked with Vinet/Murnaghan and spans of +-2/4/6%); a = (8*V0_per_atom)^(1/3)\",\n   \"ensemble\": null,\n   \"timestep_fs\": null,\n   \"n_atoms\": 8,\n   \"sim_length_ps\": null,\n   \"seeds\": null,\n   \"supercell_check_n_atoms\": 64,\n   \"bulk_modulus_GPa\": 74.5,\n   \"residual_stress_at_a0_GPa\": 0.024\n  },\n  \"flags\": [],\n  \"note\": \"PREMISE: well defined. The static 0 K equilibrium lattice constant of a perfect periodic crystal is a ground-state property that an MLIP E(V) fit can give directly. No MD, so timescale does not matter. Size: the 8-atom cubic cell and a 2x2x2 (64-atom) supercell give the same a to 1e-5 A. Forces are zero by symmetry. The residual stress at the fitted a is 0.02 GPa. ROBUSTNESS: over 3 EOS forms x 3 strain spans, a lies between 5.4556 and 5.4569 A, so the numerical/fitting uncertainty is about +-0.001 A. B0 = 74.5 GPa. VALIDATION (same model, same protocol, other elements), MACE vs room-temperature experiment from the Wikipedia 'Lattice constant' table (Si: CODATA 2018, 5.431020511 A at 22.5 C): C (diamond) 3.571 vs 3.567 (+0.1%); Ge 5.773 vs 5.658 (+2.0%); Al 4.060 vs 4.046 (+0.3%); Cu 3.626 vs 3.597 (+0.8%). For Si, 5.456 vs 5.4310 is +0.025 A (+0.46%). The overestimate matches the PBE training reference, since PBE (GGA) is known to overestimate lattice constants. UNCERTAINTY: the 0.03 A is the model/systematic error, set from the size of the deviation against experiment for Si and comparable validation solids (Ge is worse). It is not a statistical error, and the fitting error (+-0.001 A) is negligible beside it. CAVEATS: this is a static-lattice value. Zero-point and thermal expansion are not included, and the experimental 22.5 C value contains them. That correction is small for Si compared with the model error and was not computed here. The number is the MACE-MP-0 (approximately PBE-level) prediction, not an independent prediction of experiment. The Cu reference in the cited table (3.597 A) is lower than other commonly quoted values, so treat the Cu check loosely. I could not retrieve published PBE lattice constants to check MACE against its DFT parent directly. The run used mace-torch through ASE, not nvalchemi dynamics stages, because a static single-point scan needs no integrator. Raw results are in /work/eos_results.json and the script is /work/scripts/eos.py.\"\n },\n \"investigation_id\": \"\",\n \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-31T21:49:33.308936+00:00\",\n \"content_hash\": \"1785f3471780319639c5f8519ff737c667376ed4292b4ba5697615889d9ce6bc\",\n \"parent_artifact_ids\": [\n  \"4e9460a5-f9e3-4589-bc43-fd28aefbd0ba\"\n ],\n \"result_quality\": \"ok\",\n \"needs\": [],\n \"summary\": \"silicon (diamond cubic) lattice_constant = 5.456 angstrom via ASE 3.29 EquationOfState + mace-torch 0.3.15 ASE calculator (GPU, ALCHEMI toolkit environment)/MACE-MP-0 medium (2023-12-03-mace-128-L1_epoch-199), float64; trained on MPtrj (PBE/PBE+U) static 0 K E(V) scan: 11 isotropic strains of the 8-atom cubic cell, a in [0.96,1.04]*a_guess; 