{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LpBprXqpisaK2Vnr54MJNf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"silicon PBE lattice constant 5.47 Å Haas Tran Blaha 2009 calculation of lattice constants of solids\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Semiconductor Physics: A Density Functional Journey\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.13050\"},{\"title\":\"Systematic investigation of a family of gradient-dependent functionals for solids\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1003.2530\"},{\"title\":\"calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal 47and4fs7z\",\"url\":\"https://typeset.io/pdf/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-47and4fs7z.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal functionals\",\"url\":\"https://www.bohrium.com/paper-details/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-functionals/811872347643445248-529\"},{\"title\":\"Dissemin is shutting down on January 1st, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dissem.in/p/27732682/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-functionals\"},{\"title\":\"accurate band gaps of semiconductors and insulators with a 1nnqe1ie65\",\"url\":\"https://typeset.io/pdf/accurate-band-gaps-of-semiconductors-and-insulators-with-a-1nnqe1ie65.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"nih.gov\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3331871\"},{\"title\":\"Assessing the performance of recent density functionals for bulk solids\",\"url\":\"https://www.bohrium.com/paper-details/assessing-the-performance-of-recent-density-functionals-for-bulk-solids/811858929981063168-529\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1102.1358.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"workhorse semilocal density functional for condensed matter 3w8j6byd0v\",\"url\":\"https://typeset.io/pdf/workhorse-semilocal-density-functional-for-condensed-matter-3w8j6byd0v.pdf\"}]\n\nThe search confirmed the Haas, Tran, and Blaha paper but did not return its silicon value, so I can't verify the 5.47 Å figure from that paper directly.\n\n- **The paper:** Haas, Tran, and Blaha, \"Calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal functionals,\" was published in Physical Review B 79, 085104 in 2009. It assessed LDA, several GGAs including PBE, and TPSS on a set of 60 cubic solids, using the WIEN2k code. Received 5 November 2008; published 10 February 2009, and the performances of the LDA, GGA (PBE, AM05, WC, PBEsol, and SOGGA), and TPSS functionals for the lattice constants and bulk moduli were assessed on a set of 60 cubic solids.\n- **The 5.47 Å value:** A 2020 arXiv review (arXiv:2010.13050) lists a PAW-based PBE lattice constant of 5.467 Å for Si (diamond structure), against an experimental value of 5.430 Å. That is consistent with your 5.47 Å figure, but it is a different source from the 2009 paper.\n- **General PBE trend:** The same review notes that PBE consistently overestimates the lattice constants for semiconductors. Other sources describe PBE as giving reasonable but too-long lattice constants.\n\nNext step: to confirm the exact Si value in the 2009 paper, the full text (Phys. Rev. B 79, 085104, DOI 10.1103/PhysRevB.79.085104) would need to be checked, since the search results only gave its abstract-level content.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4424dcd7-704f-4825-9183-3762f46c53b5","uuid":"b74e2d4a-5090-4ecd-b0f0-1c58920d8c8e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:52:12.803Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"silicon PBE lattice constant 5.47 Å Haas Tran Blaha 2009 calculation of lattice constants of solids","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NdST1iWLf2W2srx4thpNAZ","content":[{"title":"Semiconductor Physics: A Density Functional Journey","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.13050"},{"title":"Systematic investigation of a family of gradient-dependent functionals for solids","url":"https://arxiv.