t of 60 cubic solids.\n- **The 5.47 Å value:** A 2020 arXiv review (arXiv:2010.13050) lists a PAW-based PBE lattice constant of 5.467 Å for Si (diamond structure), against an experimental value of 5.430 Å. That is consistent with your 5.47 Å figure, but it is a different source from the 2009 paper.\n- **General PBE trend:** The same review notes that PBE consistently overestimates the lattice constants for semiconductors. Other sources describe PBE as giving reasonable but too-long lattice constants.\n\nNext step: to confirm the exact Si value in the 2009 paper, the full text (Phys. Rev. B 79, 085104, DOI 10.1103/PhysRevB.79.085104) would need to be checked, since the search results only gave its abstract-level content."],"durationSeconds":5.091565424000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LpBprXqpisaK2Vnr54MJNf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
